<!--
  BlockML VS Code — Marketplace listing copy

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.vscode.documentation.MarketplaceListing
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.vscode.documentation"
  xmlns:theme="org.blockml.bml.vscode.theme"
  xmlns:vscode="org.blockml.bml.vscode">

  <name>MarketplaceListing</name>
  <type>doc:MarketplaceListing</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A VS Code Marketplace / Open VSX listing description</is>

  <documentation>
    SSOT for the published extension listing. Generators emit README.md at the repository root from
    this Block. CHANGELOG.md is maintained beside it as the Marketplace changelog tab. Do not treat
    vscode:README as the Marketplace page — that Block is the library reading entry for LLMs.

    Listing intent (V1):

    Headline: Language support for BlockML (BML) in Visual Studio Code and Cursor.

    V1 limitation (must appear near the top): This is a V1 release with limited syntax support.
    There is no language server yet, so the editor does not provide diagnostics, completions,
    hover, rename, or go-to-definition. Highlighting is TextMate-only (structure and position-based
    tag roles). A BlockML language server and richer IDE features are planned for V2.

    V1 features to list:
    • .bml file type (language id bml)
    • Position-based syntax highlighting for framework vs domain tags
    • BlockML color theme (id blockml) — required for visible coloring; generic Dark+/Light+
      themes do not paint the *.bml TextMate scopes
    • BlockML file icons (icon theme blockml-icons)
    • XSD: language bml is an xmlLanguageParticipant so vscode-xml still honours
      xsi:schemaLocation (https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd). Install XML by Red Hat
      for schema validation / completion. The BlockML color theme also paints XML/XSD
      TextMate scopes so .xsd files stay readable.

    How to enable the theme: Command Palette → Preferences: Color Theme → BlockML.

    V2 (upcoming, not in this package): language server, semantic highlighting, and Java-like
    navigation between BML files.

    License: Apache-2.0. Gallery icon: icons/blockml.png (PNG, not SVG).
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="doc:V1Scope" relation="Requires">
      V1 feature set described on the listing.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:V2Scope" relation="SeeAlso">
      Upcoming language server and IDE features.
    </see>
    <see type="theme:BlockMlDevColorTheme" relation="SeeAlso">
      Shipped color theme users must select.
    </see>
    <see type="vscode:BlockMlExtension" relation="SeeAlso">
      Extension identity (publisher, displayName, description).
    </see>
    <see file="README.md" relation="Generates">
      Marketplace page body rendered from this Block.
    </see>
    <see file="CHANGELOG.md" relation="SeeAlso">
      Marketplace changelog tab.
    </see>
    <see file="icons/blockml.png" relation="Requires">
      Marketplace gallery icon (package.json icon).
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
